<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 17 May, from 1395 to 1973.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mircea-the-elder" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mircea-the-elder.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1395">1395 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">631 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mircea the Elder holds the field against Bayezid I at Rovine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mircea-the-elder">Mircea the Elder of Wallachia</a> met the invading Ottoman army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Sultan Bayezid I</a>, which heavily outnumbered his own and included Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>, at Rovine. Though the outcome is disputed, Mircea held the field and Wallachia preserved its autonomy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rovine">Battle of Rovine</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Duke of Buckingham is executed for treason</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stafford">Stafford</a>, Duke of Buckingham, was beheaded on Tower Hill after a trial for allegedly plotting against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>. His fall showed how dangerous royal blood had become under the Tudors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1536">1536 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">490 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII's marriage to Anne Boleyn is annulled</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s marriage to Anne Boleyn, his second wife and Queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> since 1533, was annulled. The circumstances of her marriage and execution for treason made her a key figure at the start of the English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1590">1590 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">436 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anne of Denmark is crowned queen of Scotland at Holyrood</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, who had married King James VI in 1589, was crowned Queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holyrood-abbey">Holyrood Abbey</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>. Her ceremonial entry into the city, with spectacle, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and allegorical tableaux, followed on 19 May.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holyrood-abbey">Holyrood Abbey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1673">1673 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">353 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jolliet and Marquette set out to explore the Mississippi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-jolliet">Louis Jolliet</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-marquette">Jacques Marquette</a> left St Ignace with five companions in two canoes. They travelled down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkansas">Arkansas</a> River, mapping it for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brokers sign the Buttonwood Agreement on Wall Street</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Twenty-four brokers agreed to trade securities among themselves at a fixed commission. Their pact, traditionally signed under a buttonwood tree, is the origin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Stock Exchange.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1954">1954 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">72 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Supreme Court strikes down school segregation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Brown v. Board of Education the US Supreme Court ruled unanimously that racially segregated public schools were unconstitutional, overturning the 'separate but equal' doctrine in education.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Senate Watergate hearings open on television</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate committee began televised hearings into the Watergate break-in and cover-up. Testimony revealed the White House taping system, which led to Nixon's resignation in August 1974.</p></div></li></ol>
